<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Freiburg im Breisgau</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Freiburg im <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/breisgau">Breisgau</a> is a city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden-wurttemberg">Baden-Württemberg</a>, south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, on the edge of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-forest">Black Forest</a>. Founded by the Zähringen dukes in 1120, it passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a> in 1368 and was the chief town of Further <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>, later its seat of government, until it went to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden">Baden</a> in 1805–1806. Its university was founded in 1457, and its Gothic minster is a landmark.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/freiburg-im-breisgau.jpg" alt="Freiburg im Breisgau" width="320" height="279" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: C. M. · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Freiburg_im_Breisgau_M%C3%BCnster.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
